# terraria (translated client): first start up to the world (as g6_enter_world.input), then window events in play:
# focus lost / gained, minimise / restore, resizes, Alt+Enter twice, the cursor outside the window.
frame 900 mouse 640 360
# "English" is the first entry of the language list (first run only: no config.json yet)
frame 1010 mouse 640 247
frame 1030 click left
frame 1100 mouse 900 600
# hover "Single Player" (highlight + tick sound), then click it
frame 1210 mouse 640 250
frame 1250 click left
frame 1330 mouse 900 650
# "New" on the player select screen
frame 1410 mouse 807 650
frame 1430 click left
frame 1500 mouse 1100 680
# "Create": the name prompt opens; type a name and confirm
frame 1570 mouse 770 533
frame 1590 click left
frame 1660 text Porter
# Enter arrives as a typed character (WM_CHAR 13): Main.GetInputText reads it from the IME key listener
frame 1700 text \n
frame 1800 mouse 1100 680
# the play button of the player's row: world select
frame 1870 mouse 348 311
frame 1890 click left
frame 1960 mouse 1100 680
# the play button of the world's row: the world loads (WorldGen.playWorld) and the game starts
frame 2030 mouse 348 311
frame 2050 click left
frame 2120 mouse 900 500
# ---- window events in play (g13): none of them may stop the game
frame 2390 dump player
# the window loses the focus for two seconds, then gets it back (Game.Deactivated / Activated, Main.hasFocus)
frame 2400 focus lost
frame 2460 shot ../work/shots/g13a_focus_lost.png
frame 2520 focus gained
# walk a little so that input after the focus change is seen
frame 2540 key D down
frame 2600 key D up
# minimise for two seconds (inactive, nothing is drawn), restore
frame 2620 minimise
frame 2740 restore
frame 2800 shot ../work/shots/g13b_restored.png
# resize down, up, and to an odd size
frame 2820 resize 1024 600
frame 2900 shot ../work/shots/g13c_1024x600.png
frame 2920 resize 1600 900
frame 3000 shot ../work/shots/g13d_1600x900.png
frame 3020 resize 1281 721
frame 3080 resize 1280 720
# Alt+Enter: the game's own full-screen toggle (Main.ToggleFullScreen -> GraphicsDeviceManager); twice
frame 3100 key LeftAlt down
frame 3105 key Enter press
frame 3110 key LeftAlt up
frame 3200 shot ../work/shots/g13e_fullscreen_request.png
frame 3220 key LeftAlt down
frame 3225 key Enter press
frame 3230 key LeftAlt up
# the cursor leaves the client area and comes back
frame 3300 mouse -50 -50
frame 3340 mouse 2000 900
frame 3380 mouse 640 360
# focus lost while a key is held, regained
frame 3400 key A down
frame 3420 focus lost
frame 3480 focus gained
frame 3500 key A up
frame 3560 dump player
frame 3570 shot ../work/shots/g13f_end.png
frame 3600 quit
